      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had initially intended to do this with `ATOMIC_DEFINE`, which takes a number of bits, and that would have taken `PD_STATUS_EVENT_COUNT` as an argument. However, that would have changed the data type, and the accessor functions would have had to redo the number-of-bits calculation or specify the array length directly, leaving the potential for inconsistency later. I couldn\u0027t see a way to do it idiomatically, and it seemed like it would be very verbose regardless.\n\n`ATOMIC_INIT` just takes the initial value as an argument, which I believe should be 0 regardless of the number of flags.\n\nThere\u0027s no longer a direct need for `PD_STATUS_EVENT_COUNT` with this mechanism, but I thought it might be a useful thing to have around. I could remove it, though.",
